data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** Cas9 with a guided RNA cuts DNA at a chosen site. The cell's repair then either disrupts the gene or, if a template is supplied, adds new DNA [7][3].\n- **Main uses:** Researchers commonly knock out genes and can replace disease-causing mutations with healthy sequences [2].\n- **Expanding scope:** The system derives from a bacterial antiviral defense [1][7]. It now extends to large-scale DNA transfer between bacteria [4] and has eliminated HIV in cell culture [6]."}

